  "description": "The international relations major exposes students to the theory and practice of global politics, developing capacities for analyzing international institutions and the global economy, advocating for human rights, and resolving conflicts from a Christian perspective. Whether at home or abroad, students will be professionally prepared for careers ranging from diplomacy, international law, and international business to nonprofit humanitarian work. Overlap Policy This program may not be combined with the political science major or political science minor.",
